From 04f1ab235814b7eed9ea9b075bb9dece7753ddb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:33:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 057/144] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: describe CPU performance
 capacities

The two Oryon clusters have different performance per MHz and frequency
ceilings. Without capacity data the scheduler assigns every CPU capacity
1024, hiding the faster cluster from asymmetric placement.

Use the CPU capacity values from Qualcomm's SM8750 device tree, also
present in the OnePlus 13 runtime tree: 1792 for CPUs 0-5 and 1894 for
CPUs 6-7. The architecture topology code combines these with the policy
frequency reference when normalizing scheduler capacities.

Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_sm8750/blob/d50b305f7da9e14715a25120a4ac7b1a4b8b97c3/kernel_platform/qcom/opensource/devicetree/qcom/sun.dtsi

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0076-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8750-describe-CPU-performance-capacities.patch
Import-SHA256: b1f190d778523a9b4f2de0fee5b5e1005cb2fe84ca19252f7d0d1bb727d9498d
Import-Provenance: mail headers
(cherry picked from commit a34762c4c356ec6873b59766f3c96cc21d43c992)
